     No, I don't think so.  Conflict affects whether monsters
target a nearby creature instead of the hero, but doesn't
control movement rate or order.  When one monster attacks
another, the target monster has a 75% chance to immediately
counterattack if it has enough movement credit to be able to
move this turn.  But it doesn't get to make a general move,
just an attempt to hit the critter which attacked it.  And
that uses up one move's worth of movement points, so when its
own turn comes due it might have to wait til the next turn,
depending upon how much movement it had available.  I don't
think Conflict can explain why the high priestess moved four
times in a single turn.


